WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.228 --> 00:00:02.061
It's hard to imagine a more

00:00:02.061 --> 00:00:03.486
quintessentially American vehicle

00:00:03.486 --> 00:00:05.163
than the pickup truck.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.110
But this age old love affair

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.230
is about to get a shock

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.430
that could change that
relationship forever.

00:00:24.506 --> 00:00:26.960
Outside of North America

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.540
trucks with open pickup beds

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.800
are generally considered utility vehicles

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.090
for commercial use

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.283
and don't sell in particularly high volume

00:00:34.283 --> 00:00:35.805
but in the US

00:00:35.805 --> 00:00:38.137
they're practically a
cultural institution.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.320
[Commercial Announcer] Whether
you drive America's truck

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.881
there's one place you'll want to be.

00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:45.290
Pickup trucks have been
kind of the centerpiece

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:48.310
for much of the US auto market

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.694
for 60 or 70 years really.

00:00:49.694 --> 00:00:51.390
Certainly since World War II

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.223
if not earlier.

00:00:52.223 --> 00:00:54.170
They represent the highest volume vehicles

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.003
in the US

00:00:55.003 --> 00:00:56.714
and they represent the
highest profit vehicles

00:00:56.714 --> 00:00:57.728
in the US.

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.970
Had one since I was in my twenties

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.050
couldn't function doing
what I'm doing without one.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.080
This is probably

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.024
fourth or fifth truck.

00:01:08.024 --> 00:01:10.400
I've had the same model of truck

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.050
since I was seventeen,

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.260
and I'm now 52.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.826
For work, this one fits
my purposes perfectly.

00:01:15.826 --> 00:01:17.850
The numbers are staggering;

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.830
nearly one in five vehicles sold in the US

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.090
are pickup trucks.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.282
And in April 2020

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.950
for the first time ever

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.816
pickup trucks outsold passenger cars,

00:01:25.816 --> 00:01:28.965
which have been on a
steady decline for years.

00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:32.290
With reliable sales and
healthy profit margins

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.750
you would expect manufacturers

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.730
to not mess with proven formula.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.580
Because the manufacturers have this

00:01:39.159 --> 00:01:39.992
big question that they're
always fighting with.

00:01:39.992 --> 00:01:41.360
How many of our resources

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.760
do we apply to our current business models

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.450
that make money for us right now?

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.600
And how much of our
resources do do we allot

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.010
for longer term future investment?

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.580
The interest in electric trucks

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:52.413
has been building

00:01:52.413 --> 00:01:53.610
for a while in the background,

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:54.600
but as we all know

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.304
when Elon Musk makes a splash

00:01:56.304 --> 00:01:57.855
everyone kind of watches.

00:02:01.491 --> 00:02:03.886
Tesla essentially threw the first pitch.

00:02:05.056 --> 00:02:06.530
In a game that few people

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.940
outside of the auto industry

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.543
even knew was being played.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.657
And as of mid 2020,

00:02:15.657 --> 00:02:17.163
no fewer than seven models

00:02:17.163 --> 00:02:19.330
by seven different manufacturers

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:20.670
are currently in development

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.110
supported by an astounding
amount of marketing hype

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.910
for a category that has yet to deliver

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.830
a single vehicle to market.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:28.267
Seein' the world mot as it is,

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:29.560
but how it could be.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:30.678
That is how you change the world.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.300
What makes this race especially exciting

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.830
is that it isn't just a battle

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.003
between the major
well-heeled industry players

00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:41.433
but also a lineup of young companies

00:02:41.433 --> 00:02:43.595
that resemble Silicon Valley startups

00:02:43.595 --> 00:02:48.283
complete with flashy names
and headline-grabbing CEOs.

00:02:49.203 --> 00:02:51.940
Tesla has proven

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.560
that it's possible to come out of nowhere

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:54.393
as an automaker

00:02:54.393 --> 00:02:55.580
and become a real player

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:57.390
and a real force in the industry.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.040
And I think every one of them

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.009
is hoping to be the Tesla of trucks,

00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:02.022
including Tesla.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.270
I think a lot of these startups

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.770
are feeling like we don't need

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.190
to steal 50%

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:10.819
of the F-150's market share.

00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:12.240
If we can steal

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.520
four percent of the F-150's market share,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.040
we're going to sell a lot of trucks.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.780
While early adopters may be enticed

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.585
by new tech or environmental impact,

00:03:20.585 --> 00:03:21.700
the electric pickup's fate

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.750
will come down to
convincing loyal customers

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.075
that it's demonstrably better

00:03:26.075 --> 00:03:27.875
for the same or less cost.

00:03:27.875 --> 00:03:29.900
And that's where the
innovation race comes in.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.489
I saw that a model T
got 24 miles per gallon.

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:35.620
The average car

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.580
still gets about 24 miles per gallon.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.646
Physics of that recipe

00:03:39.646 --> 00:03:41.735
of pistons going up and down

00:03:41.735 --> 00:03:43.671
and routing power,

00:03:43.671 --> 00:03:45.460
you can't get past.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.210
So the only way to have a quantum leap

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.630
is to reinvent it.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.446
Typical fraternal
combustion engine vehicle

00:03:52.446 --> 00:03:55.350
will have north of 2,000 moving parts.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.441
Every moving part is a loss of efficiency.

00:03:57.441 --> 00:04:00.310
That's what's really different
about our pickup truck.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.349
It only has four moving parts.

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:03.050
The wheels.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.560
There is nothing simpler

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.320
than a motor in each wheel

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.120
and a computer watching

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.258
that motor very precisely.

00:04:09.258 --> 00:04:11.660
After 95 years

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.890
pick up trucks get about
15 miles per gallon.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.210
We've invented a pickup truck

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:17.610
that gets equivalent
of 75 miles per gallon.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.695
Five fold it's efficient.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.810
Comparing gas to electric,

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.720
one of the first things that
you notice immediately is

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.160
the delivery of torque

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.309
and how much tool there is,

00:04:28.309 --> 00:04:29.142
in an electric vehicle.

00:04:29.142 --> 00:04:29.975
There's zero lag.

00:04:29.975 --> 00:04:31.440
So as soon as you step on the throttle,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.043
you're getting instant torque.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.240
And that's great

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.890
for the type of usability

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:37.723
that you want in a pickup

00:04:37.723 --> 00:04:39.072
when you're rock crawling or off-roading

00:04:39.072 --> 00:04:41.412
or even just normal driving situations.

00:04:41.412 --> 00:04:43.392
It gives you a lot of confidence

00:04:43.392 --> 00:04:46.100
and it's really enjoyable to drive.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.120
Every night when you go home,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.120
you can plug it in

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.440
just like you plug in your phone

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.760
and it's ready to go to the next day,

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:51.843
fully charged, ready to roll.

00:04:51.843 --> 00:04:53.968
But still floating around

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.690
are concerns that have been part

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.207
of the EV debate all along,

00:04:57.207 --> 00:04:59.620
particularly around range anxiety.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.470
With electric trucks,

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.978
range can vary widely on the carrying

00:05:01.978 --> 00:05:03.216
or towing load,

00:05:03.216 --> 00:05:05.983
reducing it by up to 50% in some cases.

00:05:05.983 --> 00:05:07.222
And the notion of freedom

00:05:07.222 --> 00:05:09.583
that is heavily baked into
American truck marketing

00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:11.879
is limited by rapid
charging infrastructure,

00:05:11.879 --> 00:05:14.352
which is still far from widespread,

00:05:14.352 --> 00:05:15.975
especially in rural areas

00:05:15.975 --> 00:05:17.630
where pickup trucks are common.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.802
And then there's another factor.

00:05:19.802 --> 00:05:21.500
You personally, would you be able

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.563
to switch to an electric truck?

00:05:24.863 --> 00:05:26.338
Hard to say.

00:05:26.338 --> 00:05:28.550
It kinda all depends

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.856
on how expensive they are.

00:05:29.856 --> 00:05:32.714
I would, if it was cost effective.

00:05:32.714 --> 00:05:36.130
So how much do these trucks cost?

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.849
Well, according to what's
been announced so far

00:05:37.849 --> 00:05:39.375
there's a pretty wide range

00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:41.669
from around $40,000 in the low end

00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:43.739
to well over a hundred thousand dollars,

00:05:43.739 --> 00:05:46.460
and different models are clearly targeted

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:47.790
toward different types of customers.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:48.982
Nonetheless, that range begins well

00:05:48.982 --> 00:05:52.360
above the cheapest gas
powered pickups in the market.

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.970
Even when taking into account the current,

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.840
various federal and state level credits

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:56.891
for electric vehicles.

00:05:56.891 --> 00:05:58.420
The good news though,

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.480
is that the core technology

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.040
behind this segment, batteries,

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.505
continue to get cheaper.

00:06:02.505 --> 00:06:06.200
Since 2010 battery prices have fallen 87%.

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.499
That's lithium ion battery pack prices

00:06:07.499 --> 00:06:08.897
from 2010 to 2019.

00:06:08.897 --> 00:06:11.863
That's a really, really sharp drop.

00:06:11.863 --> 00:06:13.320
And that's starting to get you

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.640
to the point where automakers

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.370
can make and sell an EV

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.130
for a reasonable profit margin.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:19.060
For most automakers

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.030
it's still lower

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.370
than the margins they make

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:23.930
on their average internal
combustion engine vehicles.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.075
But it's certainly getting closer

00:06:25.075 --> 00:06:27.663
as we saw with Tesla Model S,

00:06:27.663 --> 00:06:29.080
start at the high end

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.190
and kind of work your way down.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.640
I think you'll see something a bit similar

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.670
with pickups is that some

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:33.510
of these that come out

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:34.460
are going to be targeted

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.300
a little at the higher end

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.480
for the first few years

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.830
until those costs come
down a little bit further.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.004
What's fascinating about trucks is that

00:06:40.004 --> 00:06:41.749
in many ways they are perfect candidates

00:06:41.749 --> 00:06:44.359
for electric, electric drive trains.

00:06:44.359 --> 00:06:45.610
They're larger.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.380
They have more space
for the battery packs.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.213
You can hide or integrate

00:06:48.213 --> 00:06:51.425
the additional cost of the
EV components into its price

00:06:51.425 --> 00:06:53.629
easier than you can, say, a compact car.

00:06:53.629 --> 00:06:55.004
I think that all

00:06:55.004 --> 00:06:57.949
will help trucks potentially succeed

00:06:57.949 --> 00:06:59.846
if you can get the end
user to go for them.

00:06:59.846 --> 00:07:02.380
One thing that companies are succeeding

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.835
at already is setting expectations high

00:07:03.835 --> 00:07:06.818
such as GM claiming a three second

00:07:06.818 --> 00:07:07.941
zero to 60 time

00:07:07.941 --> 00:07:10.822
for its thousand plus horsepower Hummer EV

00:07:10.822 --> 00:07:12.844
or Nikola offering a 600 mile

00:07:12.844 --> 00:07:14.420
estimated maximum range

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:17.390
on its hydrogen cell fuel equipped Badger.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:19.969
But delivering on the
promises of these prototypes

00:07:19.969 --> 00:07:22.116
in a mass production vehicle

00:07:22.116 --> 00:07:24.095
is a whole other challenge

00:07:24.095 --> 00:07:25.895
especially for the startups.

00:07:25.895 --> 00:07:27.650
They don't have to just make trucks.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.720
They've got to get a supply chain going,

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.355
distribution system, assembly,

00:07:31.355 --> 00:07:33.660
plants, everything.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.506
So it's relatively easy
to produce a single

00:07:35.506 --> 00:07:37.880
or even a couple

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:39.930
concept vehicles that look really neat.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.366
Building high volume electric trucks

00:07:42.366 --> 00:07:43.561
at a high quality

00:07:43.561 --> 00:07:45.880
and distributing them
throughout the country

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:46.850
or throughout the world

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:48.712
is a much bigger undertaking.

00:07:48.712 --> 00:07:51.953
Long term, they're either
gonna need a lot more money

00:07:51.953 --> 00:07:53.780
or they're going to need to align

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:54.899
with a traditional automaker.

00:07:54.899 --> 00:07:56.630
Some of the startups

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.300
have already embraced the cliche,

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.591
if you can't beat them, join them.

00:07:59.591 --> 00:08:01.240
Usually in the form

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:02.460
of a healthy contribution

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.587
to their balance sheet.

00:08:03.587 --> 00:08:06.400
Michigan-based Rivian counts Ford

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.680
among its family of investors

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.591
with a legendary F-150 maker

00:08:09.591 --> 00:08:12.382
committing half a billion dollars so far.

00:08:12.382 --> 00:08:13.665
Meanwhile, business fleet focused

00:08:13.665 --> 00:08:16.770
Lordstown motors has made its relationship

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:18.040
with a legacy brand

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.121
a little more physical.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.180
GM was closing a plant here

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.300
in Lordstown Ohio.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.341
It made Chevy Cruises

00:08:24.341 --> 00:08:26.505
and we were able to purchase a plant,

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:29.130
but most importantly, intact.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.342
So 2,000 robots

00:08:30.342 --> 00:08:33.060
four stamping presses,

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.300
full paint booth,

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:35.210
body shop,

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.393
you know, everything.

00:08:36.393 --> 00:08:37.886
There's a huge workforce around here.

00:08:37.886 --> 00:08:38.820
It's great.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.204
Generations of automotive maker.

00:08:40.204 --> 00:08:41.850
And we're going to be here

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:42.683
for a long time

00:08:42.683 --> 00:08:43.894
because this is the future.

00:08:43.894 --> 00:08:45.700
In addition to taking

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.140
over a former GM plant,

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.195
Lordstown recently announced

00:08:48.195 --> 00:08:49.520
that it will be going public

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.836
in a deal that would
net almost $700 million

00:08:51.836 --> 00:08:53.322
to fund operations.

00:08:53.322 --> 00:08:54.942
And one of its principal supporters,

00:08:54.942 --> 00:08:57.083
you probably guessed it, general motors.

00:08:57.083 --> 00:08:59.983
The next few years are going
to be particularly interesting

00:08:59.983 --> 00:09:01.245
to watch as the entangling

00:09:01.245 --> 00:09:02.637
industry alliances shake out

00:09:02.637 --> 00:09:05.338
while the different models
make it to market, hopefully.

00:09:05.338 --> 00:09:07.272
But there's more than
just corporate profit

00:09:07.272 --> 00:09:09.748
riding on the promise
of the electric pickup.

00:09:09.748 --> 00:09:12.630
Its success could be a
major inflection point

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.100
in the American adoption

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.340
of electric vehicles.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:16.530
Historically, there's been this

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:17.465
incredible mismatch between

00:09:17.465 --> 00:09:19.648
what consumers are buying

00:09:19.648 --> 00:09:20.660
in North America,

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.037
which is far more trucks and SUVs.

00:09:22.037 --> 00:09:23.428
And the segments

00:09:23.428 --> 00:09:24.790
that a lot of those EVs

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:25.881
that we saw over the last
10 years launched into,

00:09:25.881 --> 00:09:27.054
which were Sedans

00:09:27.054 --> 00:09:29.067
and often compact Sedans at that.

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:30.247
So once there's compelling

00:09:30.247 --> 00:09:31.844
pickup truck options

00:09:31.844 --> 00:09:33.781
I think they're going to sell well.

00:09:33.781 --> 00:09:35.400
I'm actually pretty optimistic

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.865
that that could change
the game a little bit

00:09:36.865 --> 00:09:38.420
in the US

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.140
in terms of EV adoption

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.097
over the next five years.

00:09:41.097 --> 00:09:43.432
[Commercial Announcer] The market today,

00:09:43.432 --> 00:09:45.095
one is leaving the others behind.

00:09:45.095 --> 00:09:46.717
It's really a cool thing

00:09:46.717 --> 00:09:49.360
to disrupt something that

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.713
hasn't changed, essentially, in 95 years.

00:09:51.713 --> 00:09:53.557
I think all pickup trucks

00:09:53.557 --> 00:09:54.998
are going to go electric.

00:09:54.998 --> 00:09:56.570
There's no reason

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:57.407
for them not to.

00:09:57.407 --> 00:09:59.780
Disruption doesn't usually

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.196
happen overnight, but
rather in fits and starts;

00:10:02.196 --> 00:10:03.481
and eventually an idea

00:10:03.481 --> 00:10:05.751
that was once esoteric or whimsical

00:10:05.751 --> 00:10:07.285
or maybe even ridiculed

00:10:07.285 --> 00:10:10.250
becomes simply another reasonable option.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.311
And then one day you wake up

00:10:11.311 --> 00:10:12.683
and it's the default.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.820
I think that's what's gonna be fascinating

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:17.408
about the personal transportation space

00:10:17.408 --> 00:10:18.691
over the next 10, 15 years.

00:10:18.691 --> 00:10:20.153
We're not going to see

00:10:20.153 --> 00:10:21.445
any one dominant form

00:10:21.445 --> 00:10:24.023
of powering of power
system for these vehicles.

00:10:24.023 --> 00:10:25.550
We're going to see

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:26.770
an increased diversity in them.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.140
And I've always said

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.221
there isn't the silver bullet

00:10:29.221 --> 00:10:30.641
that's gonna solve all our problems.

00:10:30.641 --> 00:10:31.786
There's a bunch of copper bullets

00:10:31.786 --> 00:10:33.068
that add up to a silver bullet.

